event: response.function_call_arguments.done
data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":1625,"item_id":"fc_0d616c3398a5a04c016adb3a25be3c8191accaaf225784b6f0","output_index":5,"arguments":"{\"artifact_json\":\"{\\\"inference\\\":\\\"R001\\\",\\\"packet_sha256\\\":\\\"3073db439177082d7d6040347ca4ecf97a2d708a0dfa6fe2aef766f9fe9b598d\\\",\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Packet-only Audit A replay. Input boundary: the complete frozen packet.json and the declared Yui rules read for this audit; no source proof, other inference body, historical audit, or external mathematical source was used. The listed H001–H004 are treated as permitted conditional premises; source fidelity is outside this review. The mathematical argument in S001–S005 appears sufficient relative to those premises and the explicitly listed calculation allowance. The record nevertheless fails object closure: actual mathematical objects in the prose are omitted from the inventories. This is an audit failure, not a claimed counterexample to the theorem. The packet-declared SHA256 is reported; no independent carrier/hash attestation is claimed.\\\",\\\"checks\\\":{\\\"inputs\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"R001 uses exactly H001–H004, which are the packet's listed premises. The argument's parameter uses are consistent with the stated prime, characteristic, range, representation, and lattice assumptions. No external or mathlib source is invoked.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs/0\\\",\\\"/inputs/1\\\",\\\"/inputs/2\\\",\\\"/inputs/3\\\",\\\"/inference/inputs\\\",\\\"/inference/argument\\\"]},\\\"argument\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"S001 proves the characteristic-zero basis and divided-power actions using the stated sl2 relations and permitted iteration calculations. S002 checks the matrix-unit composites, including the nonvanishing binomial coefficients in Z_(p). S003 gives a local rank-one/fractional-ideal argument for J and its generator. S004 identifies the reduced basis and actions without assuming distinct eigenvalues modulo p. S005 applies the matrix units to any nonzero invariant subspace and checks nonzero dimension, including the stated edge cases. No first unsupported mathematical implication was found in the supplied prose relative to the declared premises/calculations.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"dependency_accounting\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The nontrivial mathematical steps are presented in the argument itself rather than imported by theorem name. H004 supplies the representation and admissibility facts; H001–H003 supply the numerical and characteristic restrictions. The allowed calculation description supports the explicitly described relation iteration, localization, free-module reduction, and elementary ideal argument; it is not being treated as authority for an unproved named theorem.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/logic/calculations\\\",\\\"/inputs/0\\\",\\\"/inputs/1\\\",\\\"/inputs/2\\\",\\\"/inputs/3\\\",\\\"/inference/argument\\\"]},\\\"output\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The argument establishes nonzero dimension and that every invariant K-subspace is zero or the whole space, which is the complete output criterion as stated. The basis correspondence identifies the actions relevant to the target's specified L(K)-module formulation.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/output/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"scope\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"W is introduced as an arbitrary invariant subspace at S005, and the argument treats its nonzero case; the zero case is immediate. The selected nonzero coefficient index is used to obtain every basis vector. The local generator a is introduced only after the existence/rank-one result F001, with no witness escape apparent.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/locals/10\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/11\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/12\\\",\\\"/inference/locals/13\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4\\\"]},\\\"applicability\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"There are no E/M inputs or source applications. Uses of the four H premises are compatible with their statements; the argument does not require the h-eigenvalues to remain distinct after reduction.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/inputs\\\",\\\"/inference/applications\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"statement_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"The H statements and target state their material conditions and conclusion directly. The local argument defines its notation in prose and gives the relevant basis/action formulas; it does not rely on an inherited equation number, citation, or opaque producer proof for mathematical meaning.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inputs\\\",\\\"/output/statement\\\",\\\"/inference/locals\\\",\\\"/inference/argument\\\"]},\\\"object_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"FAIL\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Reverse-checking the prose against the inventories finds omitted actual mathematical objects. Already in S001 the prose uses h, the identity operator Id, C-scalars c_i, and eigenvalue notation alpha_i, none of which appears in S001's objects list. In S002 the prose uses R and the R-algebra but R is absent from S002's objects list. S005 explicitly uses b_i, while its objects list contains e_i and omits b_i. The text also uses indexed/bound objects and operators not exhaustively represented by the relevant lists. Thus the actual prose does not close against the supplied object inventories, notwithstanding that several omitted objects have legitimate meanings elsewhere in the packet.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/0/objects\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/objects\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/objects\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"dependency_closure\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Factual steps used later are established in preceding prose within this one inference: in particular the basis/action facts in S001, matrix-unit identities in S002, and the rank-one generator existence in S003 (recorded as F001). No fact is supplied solely by an ancestor theorem, source proof, or unlisted external result. The missing object inventory entries are reported separately under object_closure.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/inference/argument/0/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/1/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/2/produces/0\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/3/text\\\",\\\"/inference/argument/4/text\\\"]},\\\"packet_replay\\\":{\\\"verdict\\\":\\\"PASS\\\",\\\"notes\\\":\\\"Fresh replay was performed from the complete packet.json and the relevant declared Yui procedure only, with no other mathematical task material. The packet alone provides the premises, full inference prose, calculation policy, declarations, and inventories needed to make the judgments above. This is a statement of the actual review boundary, not independent carrier identity, canonical-hash binding, transmitted-material readback, or runtime-isolation attestation. Packet-replay sufficiency does not cure the object-closure failure.\\\",\\\"locations\\\":[\\\"/warning\\\",\\\"/packet_sha256\\\",\\\"/inputs\\\",\\\"/logic/calculations\\\",\\\"/inference\\\"]}},\\\"findings\\\":[{\\\"severity\\\":\\\"audit_failure\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"/inference/argument/0/objects\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"S001's actual prose includes h, Id, c_i, and alpha_i, which are missing from the declared objects inventory. Further omissions occur at S002 and S005, notably R and b_i. This is the first identified failed closure; 